WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:11.160
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me all right? Teams is having one of its mornings.</v>

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:19.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, got you. Better than the traffic on the ring road. Spent twenty minutes looking at the same rear bumper.</v>

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:26.510
<v Callum Reid>You and me both. Traffic on the ring road was properly backed up when I came through.</v>

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.070
<v Jamie Brennan>Still warmer in the car than here. The heating in the portakabin seems to be mostly decorative.</v>

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:38.009
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's why you've still got your coat on. Thought you'd just arrived.</v>

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:46.049
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the weather report. Wednesday 04 November. Quick look at what's finished, then the live jobs.</v>

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.320
<v Sarah Okafor>I signed off the inspection on the line 2 guard on Tuesday. That's closed.</v>

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.200
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, saw that. Nothing outstanding on that inspection from production.</v>

00:00:57.439 --> 00:01:04.090
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I already swapped the filter on the waste heat boiler yesterday. Finished job, not carrying it into today.</v>

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:06.670
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, understood. Yesterday's work.</v>

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.849
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, I tested the FLTs yesterday and it's all fine now. That testing's done.</v>

00:01:15.319 --> 00:01:20.569
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, separate from that, I'll do the pre-use checks on the forklifts at half two.</v>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. That's the pre-use checks, not reopening yesterday's testing.</v>

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.150
<v Grace Liu>Exactly. Different thing. Just don't want those getting muddled together.</v>

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:37.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you also grease and check the bearings on the Gas Turbine 1 by 11am? Normal priority.</v>

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.730
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the Gas Turbine 1 by 11am. Normal priority, understood.</v>

00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:50.870
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, someone crackled over that. Eleven for the bearings?</v>

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.549
<v Grace Liu>That's right, by 11am for the bearings. Forklifts at half two.</v>

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:01.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Anything else from your side before we get into maintenance?</v>

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:09.319
<v Grace Liu>Just an observation: saw the pressure on the HV board dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.909
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Came back without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.750
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, on its own. Just reporting what I saw, not putting a new job on the list.</v>

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:29.400
<v Grace Liu>And we're still waiting on parts for the HV switchboard, nothing we can do until they arrive. That's still blocked.</v>

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:35.159
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, still waiting. There's no arrival update to change that.</v>

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, stays blocked. Not an action for somebody to pick up today.</v>

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:46.900
<v Jamie Brennan>Same sort of thing with the IM1. Can't get to the IM1 until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:48.939 --> 00:02:53.139
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, and there's no window agreed. Don't count that as released work.</v>

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. No allocation on that while it's blocked.</v>

00:02:57.289 --> 00:03:05.689
<v Callum Reid>Oh, and we were going to replace the belt on the line 3 barrel but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>Ah, right. That was on the old list I was looking at.</v>

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:16.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Not for today, then. That belt replacement's off this stand-up's actions.</v>

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:24.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Fire Alarm Panel by the 28th? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:33.939
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Fire Alarm Panel by the 28th. Got it as top priority.</v>

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:40.030
<v Grace Liu>Sorry, just separating those in my head—sign-off there, but who's got the permit and isolation side?</v>

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:50.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the fire panel by Thursday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:57.819
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the fire panel by Thursday.</v>

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:04.460
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so those are separate bits. I heard 'panel' twice and thought we'd crossed over.</v>

00:04:05.289 --> 00:04:09.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Separate responsibilities, yeah. Not giving the same job to two people.</v>

00:04:10.539 --> 00:04:14.740
<v Marcus Hale>And understood on the urgency—not an emergency, but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:25.459
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by the 28th as well. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that applies to mine too.</v>

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.370
<v Callum Reid>So the monthly fire alarm test is yours, Sarah?</v>

00:04:31.339 --> 00:04:34.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, mine. I'll run it by the 28th.</v>

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.019
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Cheers. Your audio dropped for a second, only caught the end of that.</v>

00:04:40.259 --> 00:04:44.810
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries. At least it dropped during me talking, which probably improved things.</v>

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:56.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one, Tomasz Nowak, can you go to the warehouse to pick up the replacement parts for the GT2 Number 2 Bearing next week? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:58.069 --> 00:05:00.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>Full name! Sounds like I'm back at school.</v>

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:07.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Only because you were laughing over me. Next week for that collection, but drop everything for that one.</v>

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:17.509
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, understood. I'll go to the warehouse to pick up the replacement parts for the GT2 Number 2 Bearing next week. That takes precedence.</v>

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:22.500
<v Jamie Brennan>That's collection only, yeah? Not fitting the bearing under the same action?</v>

00:05:23.129 --> 00:05:27.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, just picking up the replacement parts. No fitting job being added here.</v>

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.920
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fine by me. Collection only.</v>

00:05:32.079 --> 00:05:38.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you replace the seals on the booster pump by Wednesday? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:43.230
<v Jamie Brennan>Actual seal replacement, not just getting the seals out of stores?</v>

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:50.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, replace the seals on the booster pump. By Wednesday, and drop everything for that one.</v>

00:05:52.629 --> 00:05:57.879
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, accepted. I'll replace the seals on the booster pump by Wednesday. That goes first.</v>

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:01.680
<v Tomasz Nowak>Gets you out of the cold portakabin, anyway.</v>

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.689
<v Jamie Brennan>Knew there'd be a silver lining somewhere.</v>

00:06:08.079 --> 00:06:12.980
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, enough career advice from the cheap seats. Everyone clear on what they've accepted?</v>

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:18.360
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. Nothing new from me; the filter I mentioned was yesterday's completed work.</v>

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:24.819
<v Callum Reid>Clear here. And no sneaking that cancelled belt job back in from the old list.</v>

00:06:26.459 --> 00:06:30.310
<v Grace Liu>Yep, clear. My observation and the parts hold aren't extra actions.</v>

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.810
<v Marcus Hale>All clear from me too.</v>

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's us, then. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.850
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers. Ending the call before my fingers freeze to the keyboard.</v>
